---
import Legal from '../layouts/Legal.astro';
import { SITE, url } from '../lib/site';
---

<Legal title="Cancellation and refund policy" description={`How cancelling an ${SITE.name} trial or subscription works, and when you get a refund.`} updated="5 October 2026">
  <p>
    This policy covers payments to {SITE.legalName} for {SITE.name} subscriptions and credit top-ups. Payments are processed by our payment partner (Razorpay); we never see or store your full card details.
  </p>

  <h2>Free trial</h2>
  <ul>
    <li>Every plan starts with a 7-day trial. You add a card or UPI Autopay mandate to start it, and nothing is charged during the 7 days.</li>
    <li>To set up the mandate your bank may place a small verification charge (for example ₹1–₹5). The payment partner reverses it automatically.</li>
    <li>Cancel any time before the trial ends (Plan &amp; Billing → Cancel) and you will not be charged. Otherwise your chosen plan starts on day 8 and the first payment is taken.</li>
  </ul>

  <h2>Cancelling a subscription</h2>
  <ul>
    <li>You can cancel at any time in the app (Plan &amp; Billing → Cancel) or by emailing <a href={`mailto:${SITE.contactEmail}`}>{SITE.contactEmail}</a> from your account email.</li>
    <li>Cancelling stops all future charges. Your plan stays active, with its credits, until the end of the period you already paid for. There is no cancellation fee.</li>
  </ul>

  <h2>Refunds</h2>
  <ul>
    <li><b>Monthly plans:</b> a month that has started is not refunded, and there are no refunds for partly used months.</li>
    <li><b>Annual plans:</b> if you cancel within 7 days of an annual payment, we refund it, minus the credits you used at the top-up rate. After 7 days, the plan runs to the end of the paid year.</li>
    <li><b>Credit top-ups:</b> an unused top-up pack can be refunded within 7 days of purchase. A pack that has been partly used is not refundable.</li>
    <li><b>Work already delivered:</b> credits spent on posts, images, articles and other content that was generated, and posts already published, are not refundable, as with any marketing service already performed.</li>
    <li><b>Always refunded in full:</b> a duplicate charge, a charge made after you cancelled, or a charge for a period in which the service was unavailable to you because of a fault on our side.</li>
  </ul>

  <h2>How to ask for a refund</h2>
  <p>
    Email <a href={`mailto:${SITE.contactEmail}`}>{SITE.contactEmail}</a> from your account email with the payment ID or invoice number and the reason. We reply within two business days.
    Approved refunds go back to the original payment method and normally reach you within 5–7 business days, depending on your bank.
  </p>

  <h2>Questions</h2>
  <p>
    See also our <a href={url('/terms')}>terms of service</a> and <a href={url('/delivery-policy')}>service delivery policy</a>, or <a href={url('/contact')}>contact us</a>.
  </p>
</Legal>
